 "literal": "As the stars-shining sky's spreading darkness departs, / following the swift movement's nature, without failing its own course, / the strong anger-intensified fear-inspiring sun, / along with the moonlight-shining moon, as if joined to the earth, / the battling, difficult-to-oppose strength's allied kings, / on the affliction-filled battlefield, making them wither, / at the time you captured their bound drum, / deviating from its position, when struck, its strong joints shaking, / did your spear escape from shattering, O Sezhiyan, / destroying them so that their breasts-shining chests burned with grief, / with limitless lamentation as they forgot their bodies and perished, / as the widowhood of the bright-foreheaded women increased, / resembling shining black sand, beautiful and soft, / seeing the cutting of their thick, dark hair?",
 "translation": "O Sezhiyan! When you crushed the allied kings of formidable strength on the terrifying battlefield, making them wither, and captured their war-drums, did your spear escape from shattering? For, when it struck them, its strong joints shook and deviated from their position. You destroyed them so that their chests, once adorned by beautiful breasts, burned with grief. Seeing the bright-foreheaded women, forgotten of themselves in limitless lamentation for their fallen husbands, cut off their thick, dark, soft, and beautiful hair that resembled shining black sand as their widowhood increased, did your spear escape being broken?",
